11. Create and resolve a merge conflict

Steps:
    1. Create feature/employee
    2. Modify the same section of a file.
    3. Commit the changes
    4. Switch to another branch.
    5. Modify the same section differently
    6. Commit the second change.
    7. Merge the branches
    8. Git will report merge conflict

Commands:
git switch main
git switch -b feature/employee

git add .
git commit -m "1st commit"

Switch to another branch
git switch main
git switch -b feature/report

git add .
git commit -m "2nd commit"

git switch main
git merge feature/employee
git merge feature/report

To resolve the conflict:
    1. When conflict occurs, open the conflicted file in VS code and remove the conflict markers
    <<<<<<<<< HEAD
    ========
    >>>>>>>>> branch-name
    2. Save the file
    3. Stage the resolved file
    4. Commit the file

Commands:
git add resolved-filename
git commit -m "Resolved conflict file commit"
git status

12. Push the project to GitHub

