git push -u origin main

13. Demonstrate git fetch vs git pull
git fetch:
It downloads information about changes from the remote repository without directly merging those changes into the current branch.
Command:
git fetch origin

git pull:
It downloads remote changes and integrates them into the current branch according to the configured pull strategy.

Command:
git pull origin main

14. Create an annotated release tag

Steps:
    1. Switch to main
    2. Pull the latest changes
    3. Create an annotated tag
    4. Verify the tag.
    5. Push the tag to github

Commands:
git switch main
git pull origin main
git tag -a v1.0.0 -m "Version v1.0.0"
git tag
git show v1.0.0
git push origin v1.0.0

